.TH "QRUN" "1" "2026-11-12" "passerelle 0.1.0" "Passerelle host tools"
.SH NAME
qrun \- Run a program from the share in the guest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qrun
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ \fIPROGRAM\fR ]
\fIARGS\fR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a program from the share in the guest (DX\-03)
.P
qrun runs a program that lives in the shared directory, either inside the QNX
guest \- by talking to the QEMU console socket given with \-\-console \- or on
the PC itself with \-\-local. It waits for the program to finish (bounded by
\-\-timeout), replays its stdout and stderr, and returns its exit code, which
makes it usable from scripts and from ctest\-like loops.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fIPROGRAM\fR
program path, relative to the share
.TP
\fIARGS\fR ...
arguments for the program
.TP
\fB\-\-share\fR \fISHARE\fR, \fB\-s\fR \fISHARE\fR
shared directory (default: configuration 'share' = '.')
.TP
\fB\-\-console\fR \fICONSOLE\fR
guest console unix socket served by QEMU (default: configuration 'console' =
'')
.TP
\fB\-\-local\fR
run the program on the PC instead of inside the guest
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR
timeout in seconds (default: configuration 'timeout' = '120')
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-config\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
print the effective configuration (text or json) and exit (choices: text,
json)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
the program ran and returned 0
.TP
\fB2\fR
usage error, missing share directory, console or host error
.TP
\fBany other value\fR
the exit code of the program that was run
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI<share>\fR
the shared directory (\-\-share), read\-only for qrun itself
.TP
\fI\-\-console PATH\fR
the QEMU console unix socket (\-serial unix:<path>)
.SH SEE ALSO
qshare(1), fsproof(1), pbench(1), qemu(1)
